As cities quickly expand and the transportation system becomes more densely populated, the demand for intelligent and more manageable transportation systems is evolving. From handling safe navigation through very busy urban local traffic \cite{shu2025decision} to transporting people and goods within indoor environments like hospitals \cite{wang2016semi} or warehouses, traditional mobility systems face many challenges, such as perception occlusion, large-scale system management, and coordinating many traffic participants in tight spaces.


