In outdoor scenarios, as transportation systems become denser and urban traffic grows heavier, the risk of collisions and accidents has significantly increased \cite{mohan2017urban}, partly due to occluded views caused by large trucks or surrounding buildings \cite{shu2021autonomous}. Similarly, in indoor applications—such as patient transport in hospitals or baggage handling in terminals—visibility can be limited by narrow hallways. These occlusions, combined with limited communication among traffic participants, pose significant challenges to achieving autonomous mobility in modern transportation systems.

