With the rapid development and advancement of cloud computing, edge devices, wireless connectivity and mobile networks, an innovative framework has been proposed, which is the Cloud Autonomous Mobility (CAM) system. This emerging framework allows the road to be equipped with various types of sensors, the perception data collected from these sensors is exchanged via high-speed communication networks and processed in the cloud to enhance the safety of traffic participants and improve the traffic efficiency\cite{jabbar2019urban}.


Prior to the emergence of CAM system, the transportation system are controlled and managed in a distributed and unconnected manner. For instance, the development of advanced driver-assistance systems (ADAS) and fully autonomous systems has aimed to improve safety through on-vehicle intelligence \cite{antony2021advanced, ning2024efficient}. %ADAS technologies, such as active collision avoidance and lanekeeping assistance, have shown promise in supporting driver behavior through enhanced perception. Meanwhile, fully self-driving systems, such as state-of-the-art autonomous vehicles \cite{ning2024efficient}, % bhatt2024watonobus
