However, the perception system is inherently limited by the range and line of sight of these sensors, leading to blind spots in critical scenarios, such as making a left turn with an oversized truck blocking the view. Additionally, equipping vehicles with high-end sensors like LiDAR and radar is costly, making vehicle-only perception less cost-effective for ensuring traffic safety.


