In this recently proposed CAM system, each end unit is connected through the cloud and the system is managed in a centralized manner. %; thus, each part of the system is able to communicate within the cloud network, making the system a fully interconnected network. 
Thanks to the remarkable 5G communication technology, the CAM system is able to achieve low-latency, high-bandwidth, and stable connections between vehicles, RSUs, and the cloud.

The nature of the cloud-based architecture offers more flexibility to the system. Given the cloud-based architecture, the system is more modularized, allowing more RSUs to integrate comparatively easily and seamlessly. As the transportation network increases and the size of urban areas increases, the system is more feasible to expand \cite{salahuddin2014rsu}. Additionally, by implementing advanced communication technologies, the cloud is able to talk to all the units with lower latency, higher reliability, and much richer information, which is very important for real-time required functions, such as danger warnings \cite{5gamericas2018urllc}. Finally, with advanced encryption and centralized security protocols, the CAM system is able to be equipped with much stronger cybersecurity, which is a concern that is drawing people's attention in these technologies \cite{bauskar2023advanced}.

Due to the advanced features of the CAM system, and to the best of our knowledge, there are limited large-scale real-world applications of the CAM system. In this paper, a CAM system that is equipped with multiple roadside units (also known as sensor nodes), implemented in the real world for both outdoor and indoor environments, is presented. This system overcomes the challenges of implementing CAM systems in the real world, such as smart device and data management, high-efficiency communication configuration, multi-input perception integration, and energy and power management.

The rest of the paper is organized as follows: Section~\ref{Chap: Framework Overview} provides an overview of the proposed CAM system; Section~\ref{Chap: Outdoor application} introduces the outdoor implementation of the CAM system; and Section~\ref{Chap: Indoor application} introduces the indoor implementation. Finally, Section~\ref{Chap: Conclusion} presents a conclusion as well as future outlook.

