In the experimental hardware setup (Fig. \ref{Connection_Overview}), two rotary, incremental encoders are sampled and decoded on an ATmega328 Arduino UNO micro-controller. The encoders provide direct measurements of the horizontal and vertical angles. A single-pole low-pass filter with the cut-off frequency at 20 Hz is cascaded with the encoder feedback to attenuate the signal noise. The high-level controller is implemented on a PC with Intel i7-10750H CPU communicating with the UNO via a serial communication line at 9600 baud rate and 100 Hz. The UNO sends a data packet of two floats (8 bytes) at a rate of 120 Hz.

